arch/riscv/mm/init.c (XIP create_kernel_page_table): map the RAM data region
PAGE_KERNEL_EXEC in the EARLY page table, not only in setup_vm_final's linear
map. .text..fast lives between _sdata and _edata; with the early mapping
non-executable, any RAM-text function reached before setup_vm_final took an
instruction page fault whose handler (traps.c __trap_section, .text..fast)
faulted too, recursing until the init stack overflowed below _sdata. Black box
2026-09-23: lastpc_before_exc=handle_exception+0x18, sp=_sdata-0xa0. This is
why spinlock.o and sched_clock.o "failed to boot" in RAM text. Perf-plan
2026-09-23 C18 (enabler for C39 function-granular RAM text).
